# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the JSON Academy Next.js project following the official Vercel documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (version 2.0.1)
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the dependency tree

### 2. Code Changes
**Modified: `app/layout.js`**
- Added import for Analytics component: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component to the root layout's body, positioned alongside the existing `<SpeedInsights />` component
- Fixed missing semicolon on the SpeedInsights import statement for code consistency

## Implementation Details

This is a Next.js 16.2.9 project using the App Router architecture. According to the official Vercel documentation (retrieved from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), the Analytics component should be added to the root layout file for App Router projects.

The implementation follows the documented pattern:
1. Import the Analytics component from `@vercel/analytics/next`
2. Add the `<Analytics />` component within the `<body>` tag of the root layout

The Analytics component will automatically:
- Track page views
- Collect web vitals metrics
- Send data to Vercel Analytics when the project is deployed on Vercel

## Verification

- ✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
- ✅ No new linting errors introduced
- ✅ Package dependencies properly updated
- ✅ Code follows existing project patterns and conventions

## Next Steps

To start seeing analytics data:
1. Deploy the project to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Analytics → Enable button)
3. Visit your deployed site to generate analytics data
4. View the data in the Vercel Analytics dashboard

## Files Changed
- `app/layout.js` - Added Analytics component
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated dependency lock file
